{
 "version": 1,
 "title": "Pop Pluck Lead",
 "category": "80s and synth-pop leads",
 "text": "Sound: the same bright synth-pop pluck, for you to play: every note a quick, glassy 'pling' with echoes bouncing left and right.\n\nHow it's built: one oscillator's saw and pulse mixed into the Ladder filter; one envelope flicks the filter open and shut, another plucks the VCA (no sustain, so notes die away even if you hold them). A touch of Drive, a Delay and a little Reverb. Four voices, so notes can ring over each other.\n\nPlay: quick riffs and arpeggios, broken chords, staccato.\n\nTweak: the filter envelope's DECAY (longer is softer), RESONANCE (a little more 'pling'), the delay's TIME.",
